"""Build curated English adaptations from the Telegram editorial archive."""
import json
from html import escape
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).parent
BASE='https://terralogicx.com'
STORIES=[
 {'slug':'grid-requests-versus-deliverable-power','title':'Grid Requests Are Not Deliverable Power','summary':'Why a connection application is only the beginning of data center infrastructure due diligence.','source_id':'2026-10-22-grid-queue','original_date':'2026-10-22','body':[
 ('The queue is a pipeline, not a power supply','A data center connection request expresses an intention to consume electricity. It does not, by itself, establish that a project controls its site, has secured a customer, can fund network upgrades, or will receive power on its proposed schedule.'),
 ('What the reporting shows','Reporting by TechRadar, drawing on Wood Mackenzie and The Wall Street Journal, describes widespread duplication and uncertainty in US data center connection requests. It also describes utilities requiring collateral and stronger contractual commitments. These are reported pipeline estimates, not measurements of operating capacity. A low-confidence request should not automatically be classified as fraudulent or commercially worthless.'),
 ('What an investor should verify','The useful question is not simply whether an application exists. Review site control, the utility study stage, required network upgrades, deposits and security obligations, easements, permits, and the conditions governing the proposed energization date. Distinguish indicative correspondence from executed agreements.'),
 ('The trade-off','Financial security can discourage speculative applications and reduce the risk that other customers pay for unused infrastructure. It can also raise barriers for smaller developers with credible projects. Screening is not a substitute for examining each project.'),
 ('Takeaway','A nearby substation and a queue position are starting points for investigation, not proof of deliverable power. Land valuation should reflect the evidence supporting connection, its cost, and its timing.')],
 'sources':[('Industry reporting: TechRadar / Yahoo Finance','https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/know-whats-real-us-utilities-011000916.html')]},
 {'slug':'three-clocks-of-ai-infrastructure','title':'The Three Clocks of AI Infrastructure','summary':'Debt service, equipment replacement, and energization must work on the same financial timeline.','source_id':'2026-10-23-ai-infrastructure-economics','original_date':'2026-10-23','body':[
 ('One sector, different business models','Hyperscalers, GPU-cluster operators, and equipment suppliers participate in the same infrastructure buildout but carry different risks. Treating them as a single category of AI beneficiaries hides where capital is committed and when cash can return.'),
 ('Clock one: financing','Debt service and other contractual payments follow their own schedule. A delayed launch does not necessarily delay those obligations. Underwriting should examine liquidity, financing conditions, and the cash required before commercial operation.'),
 ('Clock two: equipment','Compute hardware has an economic life influenced by performance, energy efficiency, customer needs, and resale value. There is no universal replacement deadline. Delayed deployment can reduce the period available to earn a return, but the effect must be modeled for the actual equipment and workload.'),
 ('Clock three: energization','The power-delivery schedule depends on more than construction inside the fence. Utility upgrades, rights of way, permits, commissioning, and contractual conditions can determine when the site starts serving customers. Revenue commencement depends on the specific customer agreement; it should not be assumed to follow a universal rule.'),
 ('Suppliers have a different exposure','Selling networking, cooling, or electrical equipment avoids some risks of owning a GPU fleet. It does not remove exposure to customer funding, delivery changes, working capital, warranty obligations, or payment terms.'),
 ('Takeaway','High demand for compute does not guarantee an investable project. Align financing obligations, equipment economics, and a documented power-delivery schedule. Sector growth and investor returns are different questions.')], 'sources':[]},
 {'slug':'equipment-orders-are-not-cash-flow','title':'Equipment Orders Are Not Cash Flow','summary':'Why strong demand for power and cooling equipment does not remove execution and valuation risk.','source_id':'2026-10-23-energy-equipment-repricing','original_date':'2026-10-23','body':[
 ('Physical necessity is not a valuation','AI data centers need power equipment and cooling. That makes suppliers relevant to infrastructure spending, but does not establish that every supplier is profitable, financially resilient, or attractively priced.'),
 ('Orders, deliveries, and cash are different stages','A backlog describes contracted or expected future business under a company’s reporting definitions. Converting it into revenue requires execution; converting revenue into cash also depends on payment terms, inventory, receivables, and customer performance.'),
 ('Delays flow through contracts','A postponed data center launch may change delivery and payment schedules. The consequences depend on cancellation terms, deposits, milestone payments, and whether the supplier can redirect production. A grid delay does not automatically cancel an equipment order.'),
 ('Check the buyer as well as the seller','Customer financing and liquidity matter to suppliers. However, a falling customer share price is not evidence, by itself, that credit facilities are exhausted or invoices will go unpaid. Those claims require financial and contractual evidence.'),
 ('Expectations still matter','A company can grow while its shares decline if the market had priced in stronger results. Explaining a particular price movement requires evidence; operational observations alone do not establish market causation.'),
 ('Takeaway','Follow the conversion of orders into deliveries, margins, and cash. Essential equipment can be a strong business and still be a poor investment at the wrong price.')], 'sources':[]}
]
CSS='body{background:#0a0e14;color:#c9d1d9;font:18px/1.75 system-ui,sans-serif;margin:0}main{max-width:850px;margin:auto;padding:36px 24px}a{color:#58a6ff}h1,h2{color:#f0f6fc;line-height:1.25}h1{font-size:2.3rem}h2{font-size:1.35rem}nav{display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap}article,section.card{margin:30px 0;padding:24px;border:1px solid #30363d;border-radius:12px}.meta,footer{color:#8b949e;font-size:15px}footer{border-top:1px solid #30363d;margin-top:40px;padding-top:20px}'
def page(title,desc,path,body,schema):
 return f'''<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{escape(title)} | TerraLogicX</title><meta name="description" content="{escape(desc,quote=True)}"><link rel="canonical" href="{BASE}{path}"><meta property="og:title" content="{escape(title,quote=True)}"><meta property="og:description" content="{escape(desc,quote=True)}"><meta property="og:url" content="{BASE}{path}"><meta property="og:type" content="{'article' if path!='/news/' else 'website'}"><script type="application/ld+json">{json.dumps(schema,ensure_ascii=False)}</script><style>{CSS}</style></head><body><main><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">TerraLogicX</a><a href="/news/">News &amp; Insights</a><a href="/about/aleksey-tikhomirov/">Founder</a></nav>{body}<footer>© 2026 TerraLogicX · Land, power, and Time-to-Power intelligence.</footer></main></body></html>'''
for item in STORIES:
 path='/news/'+item['slug']+'/'
 body=f'<article><p class="meta">Infrastructure analysis · English adaptation</p><h1>{escape(item["title"])}</h1><p>{escape(item["summary"])}</p><p class="meta">Adapted from the Telegram editorial archive dated <time datetime="{item["original_date"]}">{item["original_date"]}</time>. English edition published 24 October 2026.</p>'
 for heading,text in item['body']:body+=f'<section><h2>{escape(heading)}</h2><p>{escape(text)}</p></section>'
 body+='<section><h2>Editorial provenance</h2><p>This is an edited English adaptation of a Russian-language Telegram publication, not a verbatim translation or a new company announcement. Unverified numerical claims and unsupported causal explanations have been omitted. The analytical conclusions are TerraLogicX editorial views.</p>'
 body+=f'<p class="meta">Archive reference: {escape(item["source_id"])}</p>'
 if item['sources']:
  body+='<h2>Further reading</h2><ul>'+''.join(f'<li><a href="{escape(u,quote=True)}">{escape(label)}</a></li>' for label,u in item['sources'])+'</ul>'
 body+='</section></article>'
 schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Article','headline':item['title'],'description':item['summary'],'url':BASE+path,'inLanguage':'en','datePublished':'2026-10-24','publisher':{'@type':'Organization','@id':BASE+'/#organization','name':'TerraLogicX','url':BASE+'/'},'mainEntityOfPage':BASE+path}
 folder=ROOT/path.strip('/');folder.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);(folder/'index.html').write_text(page(item['title'],item['summary'],path,body,schema))
body='<h1>News &amp; Insights</h1><p>Land, power, data centers, and the economics of physical AI infrastructure.</p><p class="meta">Selected English adaptations from our Telegram editorial archive. These pieces are edited for relevance and clarity, not automatically mirrored.</p>'
for item in STORIES:
 body+=f'<section class="card"><p class="meta">English edition · 24 October 2026</p><h2><a href="/news/{item["slug"]}/">{escape(item["title"])}</a></h2><p>{escape(item["summary"])}</p><a href="/news/{item["slug"]}/">Read analysis →</a></section>'
schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'CollectionPage','name':'News & Insights','url':BASE+'/news/','inLanguage':'en','hasPart':[{'@type':'Article','headline':s['title'],'url':BASE+'/news/'+s['slug']+'/'} for s in STORIES]}
folder=ROOT/'news';folder.mkdir(exist_ok=True);(folder/'index.html').write_text(page('News & Insights','English analysis of AI infrastructure, land, power, and data center investment.','/news/',body,schema))
print('Built news index and three English articles')
